From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:22:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: attach MCLK provider to Titan top

The CAMBIST MCLK branches cannot run with CAMCC Titan top powered off.
Attach the clock controller to that domain so its existing runtime PM
device links keep Titan powered while an MCLK is prepared.

Keep MMCX and MX as the first two domains, with their existing required
performance states. Titan has no required performance-state entry.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index 60dc29db0..b7755630a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -2124,7 +2124,8 @@ cambistmclkcc: clock-controller@1760000 {
 				 <&bi_tcxo_ao_div2>,
 				 <&sleep_clk>;
 			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>,
-					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MX>;
+					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MX>,
+					<&camcc CAM_CC_TITAN_TOP_GDSC>;
 			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>,
 					<&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
 
-- 
